===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|oonly}}, {{m|enm|only}}, from {{inh|en|ang|ānlīċ}}, {{m|ang|ǣnlīċ|t=only; singular; solitary}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*ainalīkaz}}. Cognate with obsolete {{cog|nl|eenlijk}}, {{cog|de|ähnlich|t=similar}}, {{cog|non|álíkr}}, {{cog|sv|enlig||unified}}. {{surf|+suf|en|one|ly|alt1=on(e)|id2=adjectival}}.
* Regarding the different phonological development of ''only'' and ''one'', see the note in {{m|en|one}}.

