#* {{RQ:Foote Orators|page=54|passage=But as to uſquebagh; ah long life to the liquor—it is an exhilirator of the bovvels, and a ſtomatic to the head; I ſay, Mr. Preſident, it invigorates, it ſtimulates, it—in ſhort it is the '''onlieſt''' liquor of life, and no man alive vvill die vvhilſt he drinks it.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1888|title=Papers Relating to the Foreign Relations of the United States|author=United States. Department of State|page=316|oclc=|passage=The baron had taken a great liking to the Americans and to their ways of doing things, and frequently asserted that America was the '''only''' place to live. }}
